# Plugin lockfiles are machine-local churn, not shared intent. Every machine
# rewrites them on `:Lazy sync`, so a three-way merge just produces conflicts
# with no correct answer. Resolve to the incoming/base side and regenerate.
#
# NOTE: "ours" here is the branch being merged *into* — during a `pull --rebase`
# that is upstream, so local lockfile edits are dropped. That is intended: run
# `:Lazy sync` in nvim afterward and commit the regenerated file on its own.
#
# Requires (one-time, per machine, not stored in the repo):
#   git config merge.ours.driver true
.config/nvim/lazy-lock.json merge=ours
